      "lineage": {
        "description": "Historical registry of natural disaster events in Guatemala compiled from 1530 to 2015 by CONRED and partners, disaggregated at municipal level. Data covers seven hazard types (volcanic, seismic, landslide, wind, flood, drought, and extreme temperature events) documented through administrative records and historical archives. The dataset represents observed/recorded disaster occurrences rather than hazard modeling or exposure inventories.",
